From 72a6238716a4957f0fe942082c5eab0bcf1cf652 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:05:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [profiles] Don't report stale credentials from the network
 login prompt

CDirectory::GetDirectory asks for credentials again for as long as the
prompt reports new ones. The prompt reports them when m_changed is set,
but in user and password mode it was never cleared when the prompt
opened, so it stayed set from an earlier OK or from typing. Exiting Kodi
while the prompt was open hung the GUI thread: the prompt returned at
once, still reporting credentials, the login failed and the prompt was
shown again, forever, sending the same credentials to the server each
time.

Clear the flag each time the prompt is shown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/profiles/dialogs/GUIDialogLockSettings.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/profiles/dialogs/GUIDialogLockSettings.cpp b/xbmc/profiles/dialogs/GUIDialogLockSettings.cpp
index 25476f8..1332ced 100644
--- a/xbmc/profiles/dialogs/GUIDialogLockSettings.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/profiles/dialogs/GUIDialogLockSettings.cpp
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@ bool CGUIDialogLockSettings::ShowAndGetUserAndPassword(std::string &user, std::s
   dialog->m_user = user;
   dialog->m_url = url;
   dialog->m_saveUserDetails = saveUserDetails;
+  dialog->m_changed = false;
   dialog->Open();
 
   if (!dialog->m_changed)
-- 
